<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Que</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 713 BCE (approx.) · capital Adana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Que, a Neo-Hittite kingdom of the Cilician plain around Adana, known for its horses and for bilingual inscriptions in Luwian and Phoenician.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Hittite collapse, a kingdom arose in the fertile Cilician plain, formerly <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kizzuwatna">Kizzuwatna</a>. Its people called it Hiyawa, a name some link with the Greek <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ahhiyawa">Ahhiyawa</a>, and its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adana">Adana</a>. Assyrian texts call it Que from the 9th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awariku">Awariku</a>, the Urikki of Assyrian texts, ruled with Phoenician as a prestige language beside Luwian; bilingual inscriptions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karatepe">Karatepe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinekoy-inscription">Çineköy</a> are key to deciphering Luwian hieroglyphs. Que bred horses, which the Bible says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> bought there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> campaigned against King Kate. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awariku">Urikki</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of Tiglath-Pileser III, and by 713 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> had made Que an Assyrian province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 900 BCE – 713 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:3.72%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 713 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Adana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kate, Awariku</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian, Phoenician</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hiyawa, Adanawa</dd></dl></aside></div>

